Military Awareness Symposium 2026 (MAS 2026)

Dehradun, November 16,2026: Doon International School Riverside Campus (DIS RC) in collaboration with Bhartiya Himalayan International Strategic Manch (BHISM) in a pioneering initiative to promote national security and military awareness amongst the younger generation held a daylong symposium at the school campus. The symposium was well attended by over 1000 students from ten major schools of Dehradun.

The day-long symposium brought together an eminent gathering of distinguished military veterans, senior defence professionals, strategic thinkers, academicians and students. The initiative, led by Mr HS Mann, Director DIS RC aimed to celebrate the Indian Armed Forces and explore their invaluable contributions, traditions, legacies and evolving role in safeguarding the nation’s sovereignty and security. 

A major highlight was the tri-service keynote session featuring Lt Gen A K Singh, PVSM, AVSM, YSM, SM, VSM, PhD (Retd), head of BHISM; Rear Admiral Mukul Asthana, NM (Retd), Indian Navy; and Air Cmde Amul Kapoor, VM (Retd), Indian Air Force. Their addresses offered valuable perspectives on military leadership, operational preparedness, strategic priorities and the changing dimensions of national security.

The programme also featured specialised presentations on significant military operations. Maj Gen Sanjay Sharma, VSM (Retd), presented insights into the Seizing of Kailash Heights (2020), while Cmde Vijaypal Singh Rawat, VSM (Retd), examined the Anti-Piracy Operation (2024), highlighting the importance of maritime security. Brigadier Anirban Dutta, SM, delivered a presentation on Operation Sindoor (2025), bringing into focus a significant chapter in India’s contemporary military narrative.

An important segment of the symposium was the panel discussion on Introducing Military History in Schools, moderated by Colonel RS Sidhu, SM (Retd). The panel featured Dr Ashok Kumar, former Director General of Police, Uttarakhand; Colonel Rahul Agarwal, Commandant, Rashtriya Indian Military College (RIMC), Dehradun; and educationist and author Mr Kulbhushan Kain. Student panelists Rushal Batra from the DIS City Campus and Shruti Rawal from the DIS Riverside Campus added valuable young perspectives. The discussion explored the relevance of military history/ national security awareness in school education, highlighting its connections with leadership, geography, diplomacy, courage, sacrifice and responsible citizenship.

The symposium also featured an interactive presentation, "Think Differently – The Military Way", by Colonel Sidhu, encouraging students to appreciate the importance of critical thinking, adaptability, discipline and decisive leadership in everyday life.

Through this landmark initiative, DIS RC reaffirmed its commitment to creating meaningful learning opportunities beyond textbooks and fostering informed, responsible and nationally conscious citizens. MAS 2026 served as a significant platform for dialogue between military experience and academic inquiry, bringing the wisdom of distinguished military leaders directly into the educational environment towards Viksit Bharat.

The symposium concluded with a strong message from Mr Ajith Jacob, Principal DIS RC that service to the nation extends beyond wearing a uniform and that knowledge, integrity, responsibility and excellence are equally important expressions of patriotism. 

